# ${project_name}

${purpose}

A [BOS](https://github.com/bos-agent/bos-ai) extension package (archetype: `${archetype}`):
an installable Python package whose tools register with the BOS runtime through the
`bos.exts` entry point — usable in this project and in any project that installs it.

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `.bos/config.toml` | Project configuration: agents, plugins, runtime. |
| `.bos/agents/` | Agent definitions (`.md` frontmatter + system prompt, or `.toml`). |
| `.bos/.env` | Secrets (API keys, tokens). Gitignored — never commit it. |
| `src/${pkg_name}/tools.py` | Your extensions. The `bos.exts` entry point in `pyproject.toml` points here. |
| `src/${pkg_name}/skills/` | Skills that ship with the package, via the `bos.skills` entry point. |
| `tests/` | Package tests (`uv run pytest`). |

## Run

Always run BOS through the project venv so the package is importable
(a globally installed `boscli` will not see it):

```bash
uv run boscli gateway start   # uv syncs the venv (bos-ai + this package) on first run
uv run boscli tui             # attach the terminal UI
```

First prompt to try:

> ${first_prompt}

## Develop

```bash
uv run pytest                        # test the package
uv run boscli doctor                 # check config, env, and that the package imports
```

## Publish

```bash
uv build
uv publish
```

Any BOS project that installs the published package gets its extensions and
skills automatically via the `bos.exts` and `bos.skills` entry points.
